 "strings": {
  "<symbol=button_l1>": "",
  "Locking onto Targets": "",
  "Lock onto an enemy by holding <symbol=button_r1> and strafe around with <input_device_not=KEYBOARD_AND_MOUSE><symbol=button_l_stick></input_device_not><input_device=KEYBOARD_AND_MOUSE><symbol=button_ls_up><symbol=button_ls_left><symbol=button_ls_down><symbol=button_ls_right></input_device>": "",
  "Evading Attacks": "",
  "Lock on by holding <symbol=button_r1> and press <symbol=button_batsu>": "",
  "<symbol=button_maru><symbol=button_maru>　<symbol=button_maru><symbol=button_sankaku>　<symbol=button_maru><symbol=button_shikaku>": "",
  "Attack enemies to charge up the <color=striking>EX Gauge</color> at the top-left corner of the screen. Having at least 1 segment of the EX Gauge charged will allow you to use EX Actions.\nWhenever \"<Sign:1> EX Action\" pops up onscreen (such as when an enemy is knocked down, grabbed, near a wall, or holding a weapon), press <Sign:1> to unleash one of the many <color=striking>EX Actions</color> in your arsenal.": "",
  "For starters, press <symbol=button_sankaku> while holding a weapon or knocking down an enemy and \"<Sign:1> EX Action\" is displayed.": "",
  "The Way of the <color=blue>Crane</color> and <color=red>Tiger</color>": "",
  "Yagami can utilize two distinct combat styles: <color=blue>Crane</color> and <color=red>Tiger</color>.\nCrane is particularly effective against <color=blue>large groups</color>, whereas Tiger is most effective against<color=red> a single opponent</color></color>.": "",
  "<symbol=button_down>": "",
  "You can perform a <color=striking>Wall Jump</color> by pressing <Sign:3> to sprint toward a wall.\nOn top of being able to Wall Strike by pressing <Sign:2>, you can also perform <Sign:1>/<Sign:0> attacks or even EX Actions out of a Wall Jump after acquiring certain skills.": "",
  "Press <symbol=button_batsu> to sprint toward a wall, and then press <symbol=button_shikaku> as you kick off it": "",
  "You can spend SP to boost base stats, such as Health and Attack, or learn various Battle Skills. <color=striking>There are also some skills that you must unlock by meeting certain requirements.</color> For the time being, try learning Wall Jump Finisher from your Battle Skills.": "",
  "You will receive a <color=striking>Mortal Wound</color> when stabbed, shot, or hit with <color=striking>Deadly Attacks</color> (performed by enemies with intense auras).\nThough Mortal Wounds cannot be restored by eating or using recovery items, you can treat them by either <color=green>visiting a doctor</color> somewhere in Kamurocho or using a <color=green>Medical Kit</color>.": "",
  "After charging up the EX Gauge, press <symbol=button_r2> to activate <color=striking>EX Boost</color>.\nDuring EX Boost, your attack speed is increased and you become less likely to recoil from attacks since the EX Gauge <color=striking>absorbs your damage (Even Deadly Attacks)</color>.\n\nMoveover, changing combat styles during EX Boost will allow you to cancel out of almost any movement you're doing.": "",
  "<symbol=button_r2>": "",
  "Dealing with the Keihin Gang": "",
  "Impudent <color=striking>Keihin Gang</color> members constantly prowl the streets in search of Yagami's whereabouts.\nYou can choose to ignore these goons, but deciding to teach them a lesson will net you SP and items.\n\nBe aware that the cops will come running if you take too long to win. If that happens, it's time to get the hell out of there.": "",
  "Depending on where you are in the story and how much time has passed, there may be more Keihin Gang members swarming the streets than usual. When the <color=striking>Threat Level</color> is present, your chance of encountering Keihin Gang members is higher.\n\nPowerful <color=striking>Keihin Gang leaders</color> will show up in the city as long as the Threat Level is present.": "",
  "Keihin Gang Leaders": "",
  "When the Threat Level is onscreen, not only will there be a crazy amount of Keihin Gang members \nwandering around town, but the <color=striking>Keihin Gang leaders</color> will also show up somewhere in town.\n\nIn order to reduce the Threat Level, you must either defeat those leaders or wait for some time to pass.\nIf you do manage to defeat the leaders, you'll receive a reward from some very grateful locals.": "",
  "Drinking a medicinal extract will temporarily imbue you with one form of power or another.\n\nFor starters, try using the <color=striking>Thunder Strike Extract</color>, which can be found in Items app under Recovery Items. This will let your Crane attacks break the enemy's guard.": "",
  "Go to the Recovery Items page in the Items app and use the <color=important_a>Thunder Strike Extract</color>.": "",
  "Protect Matsugane": "",
  "During this battle, enemies will attack Matsugane in an attempt to help Hamura. <color=striking_blk>If Matsugane's health runs out, the game will end.</color> Be aware of your surroundings and protect Matsugane.": "",
  "Protect Mafuyu": "",
  "During this battle, enemies will target Mafuyu. <color=striking_blk>If Mafuyu's health runs out, the game will end.</color>\nMafuyu will cheer Yagami on, replenishing his <color=green>health</color> and </color>EX Gauge</color>, so be sure to keep her safe.": "",
  "Call In the Squad": "",
  "Raising your friendships with the locals will allow you to perform EX Bonds with some of them.\nEX Bonds work the same way as normal EX Actions, but they can only be triggered at the specific location your ally is.\nSo if you find someone in town that you think would make a good ally, definitely get them on your side.": "",
  "Press <Sign:3> while moving to sprint.\nYagami will keep sprinting, so no need to hold it down!": "",
  "<symbol=button_batsu>": "",
  "Move the cursor over something or someone you wish to examine and press <symbol=button_r2> to take a closer look.": "",
  "Street Battles": "",
  "Degenerate lowlifes, ruthless thugs, and all sorts of other scoundrels constantly roam the streets in search of a fight.\nYou can choose to run away from or outright ignore these thugs, but teaching them a lesson will net you some SP and the occasional item.\nBe warned that the cops will show up if your fights take too long, so leave the area immediately if you don't want to end up in jail.": "",
  "Once you're done inspecting everything relevant to the case, press <symbol=button_cancel> to finish your investigation.": "",
  "Use <input_device_not=KEYBOARD_AND_MOUSE><symbol=button_l_stick> or <symbol=button_up><symbol=button_down></input_device_not><input_device=KEYBOARD_AND_MOUSE><symbol=button_ls_up><symbol=button_ls_down></input_device> to select <color=striking>Work Clothes</color> and press <symbol=button_decide> to change into them.": "",
  "<symbol=button_shikaku>": "",
  "<symbol=button_sankaku>": "",
  "Your target may start to act more cautiously, as if they suddenly have an inkling that they're being watched.": "",
  "If the target sees you when this happens, the Caution Gauge will start spiking. Failing to get out of sight in time will cost you the mission.": "",
  "Your target won't be able to find you while you're taking cover, so press <symbol=button_maru> to hide behind a<color=yellow> Cover Spot</color>.": "",
  "You won't be able to move while hiding, so find the right time to <color=yellow>emerge</color> by pressing <symbol=button_maru> so your target doesn't completely slip away.": "",
  "Move the cursor over the person you wish to examine and hold <symbol=button_r2> to take a closer look.": "",
